fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1039", description: some(value: "A rule-body reflect form's INTERIOR still carries no source span, so a diagnostic raised on a NESTED dot renders '1:1' - a wrong location, not a missing one. WI-1035 closed the ROOT: 'build_body_atom_occurrence_inner' falls back to 'materialize_from_handle' for entity and reflect-form atoms, spans there come from 'kb.term_span', and a rule-body term has no entry, so 'respan_root' now stamps the atom with the parse span the loader is already holding. That reach is the root ONLY - the loader's native walk never descends into a reflect form, so no caller holds a parse span for what is inside one. MEASURED as the shape that reaches it: the receiver of a 'dot_apply' is itself materialized, so the INNER dot of a chained 'a.b().c()' in a rule body keeps SourceSpan{source: SourceId(0), span: 0..0}, which is what WI-1035's own refusal rendered as '1:1' before the root fix. Every rule-body diagnostic keyed on such a node is affected, not only the supplier tie: 'DotDispatchNoMatch', the WI-602 value-precondition refutation, and any type error inside the dispatched form. 'build_body_atom_occurrence''s doc has recorded this loss since WI-246 ('rule-body terms get no term_spans entry, so materialize gave them empty_span') and names 'narrowing these fallbacks ... native entities / structural reflect patterns' as later work WITH NO TICKET - WI-246 is delivered, so nothing owns it. NOT 'create_occurrence': 'convert_term' is hash-consed and 'term_spans' is first-write-wins, so a rule-body term interning equal to another site's term would either be denied its own span or poison that site's - the exact hazard WI-458 gave rule HEADS their own 'rule_head_span' side-table to avoid. A span is per-OCCURRENCE; only the occurrence tree can hold a per-site answer. WORK: either build reflect-form occurrences NATIVELY in 'build_body_atom_occurrence_inner' (the narrowing WI-246 names, which also fixes the entity-arm var-sharing constraint that forced the fallback), or thread a parse-span map through 'materialize_from_handle' so each materialized node can be stamped. ACCEPTANCE: a diagnostic raised on the inner dot of a chained rule-body call reports the inner dot's own line:col, asserted against the offset the needle really has in the fixture (the weaker 'is it numeric / does it differ' assertions both pass on '1:1' - MEASURED in WI-1035). REFERENCE: WI-1035; WI-246; WI-458; docs/design/058-implementation.md S21."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-07T06:12:35Z"))
